<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!-- The one process everything else depends on, and the only one nothing was watching.

         On 2026-11-08 OpenD exited cleanly after 23 days up, nothing restarted it, and the sweep
         failed 646 times over 2h42m. The market was shut, so it cost nothing — which was luck
         rather than design. Both optionality agents are managed by launchd and the thing they
         both depend on was a hand-started desktop app.

         A TIMER rather than KeepAlive, which is the whole design decision here. KeepAlive watches
         the process it launched, and `openD.sh` starts OpenD in the background and returns — so
         launchd would see the script finish a second later, conclude the job ended, and run it
         again. Immediately. For ever.

         More importantly, KeepAlive can only see whether a process EXISTS. An OpenD sitting at a
         login prompt with its websocket port shut looks perfectly healthy to the operating
         system, and that is the failure that matters: the service would show dashes while launchd
         reported everything fine. `openD.sh ensure` waits for the API port and pings the telnet
         console to confirm there is an upstream session, so it can tell the two apart. The script
         is the part that knows something; this agent is just a clock.

         A minute's granularity against the 2h42m it replaces. -->
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.optionality.opend</string>
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>__HOME__/openD.sh</string>
        <!-- idempotent and quiet when all is well: starts a dead OpenD, restarts a husk whose API
             port is shut, and only REPORTS one that is up without a confirmed session — because
             that may need a human at the login window, and a restart a minute against an expired
             credential is a watchdog flapping a provider. -->
        <string>ensure</string>
    </array>
    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>__HOME__</string>
    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <!-- launchd starts with a bare PATH, and `ensure` reaches for python3, nc and pgrep -->
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
    </dict>
    <!-- at login, and then every minute -->
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>
    <key>StartInterval</key>
    <integer>60</integer>
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>__HOME__/Library/Logs/optionality-opend.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>__HOME__/Library/Logs/optionality-opend.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
